WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:00.987
Try it.

2
00:00:00.987 --> 00:00:06.088
Lab 1 runs in PowerShell 7 on the kit's four
fictional applications, with no tenant.

3
00:00:06.088 --> 00:00:09.593
Go to the kit's folder and make
this run's results folder,

4
00:00:09.593 --> 00:00:11.774
named for the time you start, in U T C.

5
00:00:11.774 --> 00:00:14.188
Step one scans the four applications.

6
00:00:14.188 --> 00:00:18.188
Two strings hold a stored password,
and one is already on Entra.

7
00:00:18.188 --> 00:00:22.613
Payroll web's web dot config string
uses Windows integrated authentication.

8
00:00:22.613 --> 00:00:27.819
It runs on an Arc host with Microsoft
Data SQL Client five point two point two,

9
00:00:27.819 --> 00:00:33.025
at or above the managed identity release,
so it's column A: a configuration change.

10
00:00:33.025 --> 00:00:35.993
Claims batch and reports
O D B C use drivers

11
00:00:35.993 --> 00:00:38.537
with no Entra path, so they're column B.

12
00:00:38.537 --> 00:00:41.675
Vendor H R is column C
because a vendor owns it.

13
00:00:41.675 --> 00:00:46.200
The target text there is the kit's generic
advice; the vendor's release decides.
